                    {:status :not-met
                     ;; This file already said so, under :dataspace :missing,
                     ;; about 150 lines from the path that requires it, and
                     ;; nothing joined the two. A reader checking how far this
                     ;; widening is would not have looked there.
                     :evidence "declared in this file under the :dataspace entry's :missing set"
                     :also-missing-there #{:restricted-esm-provider :wasm-aot-provider :native-aot-provider :typed-document-wire-boundary}}
                    :effect-row-integration
                    {:status :not-measurable-yet
                     :why "There is no abort ability whose effect could be propagated. This is downstream of the first precondition, not independent of it."}
                    :conformance-vectors-positive-and-negative {:status :not-met}}
                   :decided-by "adr-2608301500-guest-syntax-restrictions-classified-by-shielding-mechanism"}
   :reason "Ambient throw/try/catch is untracked non-local control flow: it exits
            scopes the inferred effect row never mentions and skips unwind
            obligations (dataspace facet retraction has no checked unwind yet).
            The ban is on the ambient form; a typed abort/exception ability whose
            effect appears in the inferred row, Unison Exception-style, is
            admissible once the preconditions land."
   :adr ["adr-2608650000-kotoba-cannot-write-has-two-kinds-decision-core-extraction"
         "adr-2608301500-guest-syntax-restrictions-classified-by-shielding-mechanism"]
   :adr-covers "Superproject ADR, amended 2026-08-30 (owner instruction): the permanent invariant is no UNTRACKED control effects; [:result T E] stays the mandatory surface on every backend until the widening preconditions land, and the ambient forms stay rejected."}
  :bounded-admission
  {:disposition :intentional-security-constraint
   :shielding-axis :resource-bounds
   :limits {:max-functions 1024
            :max-parameters 5
            :max-bindings 4096
            :max-symbol-chars 128
            :max-expression-nodes 50000
            :max-list-items 128
            :max-source-bytes 1048576
            :max-reader-depth 512}
   :reason "Untrusted and generated programs must fail closed under finite admission and execution resources."
   :adr ["docs/adr/ADR-reliability-t54-max-parameters.md"
         "docs/adr/ADR-reliability-t72-fuel-model.md"]
   :adr-covers "t54 decides :max-parameters 5; t72 decides the fuel model behind execution bounds."
   :adr-gap "No ADR decides :max-functions, :max-bindings, :max-expression-nodes, :max-list-items, :max-symbol-chars, :max-source-bytes or :max-reader-depth. Those seven limits are enforced but undecided on paper (measured 2026-08-12)."}
  :capability-only-affinity
  {:disposition :intentional-semantic-simplification
   :reason "Affine consumption is scoped to capability values; a general ownership/borrow/lifetime system is intentionally absent."
   :related-adr "docs/adr/ADR-safe-capability-language.md"
   :widening-path
   {:heads #{vector-assoc vector-f64-assoc}
    :model :single-affine-value-family
    :not :general-ownership-borrow-lifetime
    :reason "A vector handle that is dead after an update can be updated in place, and the two are indistinguishable to every observer -- so this widening does not change what a program MEANS, only which lowering a backend may choose. It is one value family, not the general system this entry declines."
    :measured-gap
    {:as-of "2026-09-01"
     :write-cost :o-of-length
     :evidence "amu/tools/kexe_loader.c checked_vector_assoc memmoves the whole vector and bump-allocates. The C comment states it: every operation that changes an element allocates rather than mutates."
     :writes-per-vector-lifetime "arena / length. KEXE_VECTOR_ITEM_CAPACITY 65536 over a 16384-item vector is FOUR writes in the life of a program, because the arena is bump-only and never reclaimed."
     :why-it-matters "An order book is a struct of arrays with about a million slots per field and a write per order (superproject ADR-2608311900). Both numbers are wrong for it by orders of magnitude."}
    :preconditions
    {:affine-analysis
     {:status :met
      :evidence "kotoba.native.affine/linear?, linear-parameter? and linear-let-thread?, 16 tests. Conservative: refuses two uses on one path, a bare reference, the handle stored into itself, a consumed name that is read again, and treats vector-drop as CONSUMING because a view whose parent is later written in place is a view of something else."
      :shapes-admitted #{:let-threaded-through-distinct-names
                         :parameter-threaded-through-tail-recursion}
      :corrected "The first version (kotoba-native 79c383fb) admitted a let that rebinds one name repeatedly, which amu refuses with duplicate let binding -- a gate nothing could ever pass -- and summed the arms of an if, which refused the shape Kotoba actually uses: a vector threaded through a tail-recursive parameter, read in the base case and consumed in the step. Both found by compiling a program rather than reasoning about one (2026-09-01, amu e96dd8c6). Fixed in kotoba-native d6ee1387."}
     :backend-lowering
     {:status :not-met
      :note "No backend consults the analysis. Nothing lowers to a store."}
     :host-abi
     {:status :not-met
      :note "kexe_context_v3 carries vector_assoc only. An in-place store is a new slot and a version bump, with the _Static_assert offsets that guard against ABI drift."}
     :arena-bounds
     {:status :not-met
      :note "The bounds below stay 4096 handles / 65536 words / 16384 items. In-place update removes the reason the arena had to be four times one vector, but raising them is a separate decision with its own fail-closed argument. An order book needs about a million slots per field."}
     :conformance-vectors-positive-and-negative
     {:status :not-met
      :note "These describe the LOWERING, which does not exist yet. Not circular with the fail-closed rule: what must not move first is the admission, and it has not."}}
    :fail-closed "Until every precondition is met, vector-assoc keeps allocating. The analysis existing changes nothing a program can observe."
    :decided-by "adr-2609010200-affine-homogeneous-vectors-so-a-book-can-be-written"}}}

